id: pm-gzyt2j
title: "2026-08-04 holistic pm CLI, SDK, and ecosystem manual review and optimization plan"
description: "Tracker-only manual review of current main across the complete CLI, public SDK, repository architecture, agent UX and token economics, performance, security, code quality, tests, docs, skills, built-in and external packages, GitHub reports, dependency posture, multi-agent merge safety, provenance, and daily npm/Bun release behavior. This session records evidence, canonical findings, sequencing, and typed relationships only; it does not implement product changes."
type: Plan
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[10]: agent-ux,architecture,audit,ecosystem,github,packages,performance,planning,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-08-04T08:36:03.297Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T09:34:43.070Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-04T09:34:05.008Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-04T09:34:05.008Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Current main, live all-status PM history, repository structure, command contracts, SDK and extension surfaces, GitHub PRs/issues/reports, dependency and vulnerability state, external pm packages, multi-agent merge behavior, and release pipeline are manually reviewed; Every confirmed gap is deduplicated against all statuses and recorded on a canonical PM item with rich metadata, evidence, and typed graph relationships; Every GitHub PR and issue in scope has a comment containing its corresponding pm item link, or a precise documented limitation if GitHub refuses mutation; No product code, tests, docs, workflows, packages, or issue implementation is changed in this session; only PM tracker planning and evidence are committed; Tracker graph, history, lifecycle, storage, duplicate state, security scan, commit scope, remote SHA equality, and hosted main checks are verified before closeout"
definition_of_ready: Required bootstrap and all-status duplicate orientation completed on current main
outcome: "A prioritized, dependency-aware, deep-linked roadmap that makes future implementation cohesive while preserving every existing capability"
why_now: Rapid SDK and CLI changes plus external packages and daily releases require a fresh evidence-backed plan before the next implementation tranche
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: completed
expected_result: "An approved, deduplicated, dependency-aware PM roadmap backed by current CLI, SDK, ecosystem, GitHub, security, performance, merge, and release evidence, with no product implementation."
actual_result: The ten-step research plan is 100% complete and approved; canonical items contain findings and typed relationships; all 28 open GitHub issues are PM-linked; remaining historical GitHub backfill and verification-context limitations have explicit open owners; only PM tracker records changed.
