comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T08:36:03.297Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: searched all-status ecosystem audit, SDK, CLI simplification, graph, package, provenance, security, dependency, release, GitHub, and agent-context terms. Closed pm-t9e3bc owns the 2026-07-26 point-in-time review; open pm-a8zm owns relationship reconstruction only; canonical epics own implementation themes. This plan is the non-numbered current-main review artifact and will create no implementation duplicates."
  "2026-08-04T09:22:18.823Z","harness:codex","Audit synthesis 2026-08-04: reviewed the live 2,310-item tracker and complete status graph; current repository and SDK boundaries; 76-command contract summary; 18-package published ecosystem; GitHub issues, PRs, alerts, workflows, releases, and dependencies; code topology, duplication, suppressions, docs, performance, retrieval, security, provenance, merge safety, and release consumers. No product implementation was performed. Canonical existing owners were updated before new work was created. New owners are limited to the six current GitHub reports, historical GitHub linkage backfill pm-w2krlt, and bounded annotation mutation output pm-9stazf."
  "2026-08-04T09:30:25.193Z","harness:codex","Linked verification boundary 2026-08-04: the first aggregate pm test run recorded 2 passes and 2 failures. Build+typecheck and published-release verification pass under the default schema sandbox. The focused merge suite passes directly 120/120 but fails linked 119/120 because the schema context adds validate_merge_driver_configuration warnings. The 10k scale gate passes directly but linked schema context fails CLI/SDK get/context token thresholds and CLI create latency. New canonical issue pm-e97jyf owns execution-context parity; these failures are preserved and are not described as product-test success."
  "2026-08-04T09:33:52.703Z","harness:codex","Final validation 2026-08-04: tracker health is OK for 2,313 items, 2,327 history streams, and 44,285 immutable events; no active or stale locks, no drift, hash/chain mismatch, parse/conflict-marker failure, tracked runtime cache, pending merge decision, or merge-driver/fence error exists. Resolution validation retains 295 classified legacy closed records missing modern resolution fields. Graph is one component with zero active isolates/degree-one nodes and 11 informational legacy findings. Duplicate scan returns the same 14 historical or intentional clusters and no new audit owner. GitHub has zero open PRs and all 28 open issues now have verified PM-link comments. Archive-wide coverage is 537 of 892 PR/issue artifacts after 113 successful backfills; GitHub secondary content-creation throttling stopped mutation with 355 closed artifacts remaining, owned by pm-w2krlt. Product code, tests, docs, workflows, and package sources were not changed."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:22:19.412Z","harness:codex","Execution order: first restore trustworthy agent feedback loops by bounding annotation writes, completing command intents/token budgets, fixing positional help recovery, and making import/transport gates statistically robust. Next preserve feature parity while decomposing SDK and CLI ownership, draining flat directories, pruning suppressions/dead exports, and unifying retrieval evaluation. In parallel harden extension composition/collision policy, automatic provenance dimensions, merge-recovery guidance, and terminal lifecycle recovery. Treat historical GitHub backfill as paced governance work and dependency majors as compatibility-gated, not urgent security updates."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:22:20.027Z","harness:codex","An isolated green package fleet proves install and activation compatibility but not multi-package composition; collision and global override semantics require an all-at-once fixture. A green current release proves the immutable artifact, not historical scheduled reliability. Deep graph quality comes from truthful typed causality and verification edges, not arbitrary density. Agent-token budgets must exercise long-lived mutation responses because small read fixtures can pass while one append emits an entire project history."
